        <headline>Cancellation of Severe Thunderstorm Warning for Pilbara, Gascoyne and South Interior forecast districts</headline>
        <description>
          
          
          This warning is now cancelled.
           
        </description>
        <instruction>The Department of Fire and Emergency Services advises that people should:
* Keep away from flooded drains, rivers, streams and waterways.
* Be careful of fallen trees, damaged buildings and debris.
* Be careful of fallen power lines. They are dangerous and should always be treated as live.
* Assess your home, car and property for damage.
* If damage has occurred take photos and contact your insurance company to organise permanent repairs.
* If your home or property has significant damage, like a badly damaged roof or flooding, call the SES on 132 500.

</instruction>
